## Reflection

If revisiting this project, several improvements would be made:

- Reevaluate thresholds used to flag high-risk users  
- Balance precision with inclusivity in model decisions  
- Expand consent options to allow selective data sharing  
- Include a more diverse group of testers earlier in development  

The ethical trade-offs in this project were complex but valuable, reinforcing the importance of integrating ethics into technical design.

---

## Key Takeaways

- Ethical considerations must be integrated from the start  
- Privacy and data minimization are critical  
- Accessibility and inclusion should be actively addressed  
- Transparency and accountability improve trust  
- Continuous evaluation is necessary to maintain ethical alignment
